# Create Multi Command

A multi command is a named sequence of smaller commands. It coordinates an ordered chain of existing commands without adding logic of its own.

## Use when

One user action must trigger several existing commands in a fixed, known order. Examples: "save and publish" (SaveCommand → PublishCommand), "reset and reload" (ClearCommand → LoadCommand).

## Good case

Composing two or more already-written commands into a single named chain. The multi command itself contains no business logic — it only declares the order.

## Bad case

Using a multi command as a dumping ground for ad-hoc logic. If you find yourself adding `if` statements or data transformation inside the multi command, split the logic into smaller single commands first.

## Key API

- Extend the multi command base class and declare the ordered list of command classes to run.
- Pass shared data between commands through the wave or a `WaveBean` attached to the triggering wave.

Template: `templates/MultiCommandTemplate.java.txt`.
